window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["19"]={"https://theconversation.com/with-two-weeks-to-go-the-victorian-election-is-the-coalitions-to-lose-296248":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"dc2bbd686f36965acf6e97056e6d350c66e514e8531bbd807e65b6737c495e43","read":"https://theconversation.com/with-two-weeks-to-go-the-victorian-election-is-the-coalitions-to-lose-296248","bytes":183741,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"With two weeks to go, the Victorian election is the Coalition’s to lose","by":[{"n":"Nicholas Barry","r":"Senior Lecturer in Politics, Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences, La Trobe University"}],"pub":"2026-11-15T17:24:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["As the Victorian election campaign enters its final fortnight, polling points to the strong likelihood of a change of government on November 28."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Coalition, led by Jess Wilson, came into the campaign with a significant lead and it has since further strengthened its position. Polling published in the ",["Australian Financial Review","https://www.afr.com/politics/victorian-coalition-position-strengthens-labor-reduced-to-rump-in-new-poll-20261111-p61d0z"]," late last week had the Coalition well ahead with 31% of the vote, Labor on 23% and One Nation on 22%, while the Greens were on 15%."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two-party preferred vote between the Coalition and Labor was 57-43 in the Coalition’s favour. Although there are small differences, other recent polls point in a similar direction."]},{"k":"p","s":["How this will translate into seats in parliament is more complex than usual because of the low primary vote of both major parties and the high numbers for One Nation and the Greens. There are many seats that are likely to be three or four cornered contests, the results for which can be ",["hard to predict","https://www.afr.com/politics/three-way-contests-could-make-a-big-difference-in-victoria-s-election-20261103-p61agd"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the campaign so far has brought the playing field into clearer focus, with each party facing their own challenges and opportunities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Politics with Michelle Grattan: Kos Samaras & Richard Willingham on Victoria’s expected change of government","https://theconversation.com/politics-with-michelle-grattan-kos-samaras-and-richard-willingham-on-victorias-expected-change-of-government-296250"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Labor falling further behind"]},{"k":"p","s":["The campaign has been difficult for Labor. Three terms in office, ",["corruption allegations","https://theconversation.com/how-the-big-build-corruption-allegations-brought-down-the-victorian-premier-288489"]," resulting in a royal commission into the construction industry, and cost-of-living pressures meant it went into the campaign well behind in the polls."]},{"k":"p","s":["It has been unable to make up the ground and has fallen further behind the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Combined with the Liberals ",["agreeing to","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/10/coalition-one-nation-preference-deal-victorian-election-labor-greens-ntwnfb"]," a preference deal with One Nation, there are predictions Labor could be reduced to a ",["“rump” in parliament","https://www.afr.com/politics/victorian-coalition-position-strengthens-labor-reduced-to-rump-in-new-poll-20261111-p61d0z"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The change in leadership from Jacinta Allan to Ben Carroll in July has made it hard for the government to run on its record. Some of its traditional strengths – infrastructure and industrial relations – are shaky territory because of the royal commission. A number of unions have ",["also criticised","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/more-unions-down-tools-in-labors-victorian-election-campaign-as-trust-broken"]," the government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor has a suite of policy announcements in a range of areas, particularly transport, housing and dental care, but a major focus of the campaign has been warning about the risks of a Liberal-One Nation minority government and claims about Wilson’s views on health care."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safe, small targets"]},{"k":"p","s":["Going in as the frontrunner, the Coalition’s aim was to consolidate and strengthen its position, while avoiding pitfalls."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson has largely managed to achieve this so far while avoiding the internal infighting that plagued the party for much of its recent time in opposition."]},{"k":"p","s":["It has also made a range of policy announcements, focusing particularly on the economy, law and order and the need to change the government."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the most part, though, the Coalition has tried to run a fairly safe and small-target campaign, oriented around Wilson. This has led to ",["criticism","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-12/victorian-election-campaign-missing-leader-debates/107374014"]," from some Liberal MPs and candidates who claim their public appearances are being too tightly controlled, in “a very presidential campaign”."]},{"k":"h","s":["A characteristically bumpy ride"]},{"k":"p","s":["The One Nation campaign has been far from smooth sailing, with ",["controversy","https://www.theage.com.au/politics/victoria/one-nation-vows-spending-transparency-but-refuses-to-release-policy-costings-20261102-p61ak6.html"]," over its decision not to get the Parliamentary Budget Office to cost its policies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party also disendorsed two candidates, one of whom ",["described Hitler as the “GOAT”","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-10/vic-one-nation-preston-candidate-guardiani-dumped/107368834"]," (greatest of all time) and made Islamaphobic comments on social media."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nonetheless, it continues to perform strongly in the polls and is close to Labor’s level of support. Combined with the Liberal preference deal, it seems likely it will win seats in the lower house as well as having a significant presence in the upper house."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party leader, Warren Pickering, ",["spoke to the Melbourne Press Club on Thursday","https://www.afr.com/politics/we-re-here-get-used-to-it-one-nation-s-warning-for-victoria-s-establishment-20261112-p61cy2"]," and echoed many of the themes associated with right-wing populist parties around the world, criticising the major parties and the media, and hinting at sinister left-wing international forces:"]},{"k":"p","s":["we don’t answer to the tired, worn-out and obsolete two-party system that Labor and the Coalition have stitched up for themselves. We don’t answer to the globalists, the Marxists, international bodies or the cult of climate change."]},{"k":"h","s":["What about the Greens?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greens campaign has focused on issues around public housing, rent controls, transport and dental care. At its campaign launch, held in early October, ",["leader Ellen Sandel said","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/09/victoria-greens-2026-state-election-campaign-launch-david-shoebridge-ellen-sandell"]," their aim was to “replace Labor” and they have targeted six inner-city Labor seats in the lower house."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party seems on track to benefit from the predicted fall in Labor’s vote and may well increase its presence in the lower house, although there is some uncertainty here."]},{"k":"p","s":["The party ",["has struggled","https://www.crikey.com.au/2026/11/12/victorian-election-the-greens-labor-vote/"]," to get as much attention in the media as the other parties."]},{"k":"h","s":["A changing party system"]},{"k":"p","s":["As well as the likelihood of a change of government, the campaign and upcoming election are of broader significance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent decades have seen a drift of votes away from the major parties, both in Victoria and around the country. In 1999, the combined Labor, Liberal and National share of the two party preferred vote in the Victorian Legislative Assembly was ",["a bit over 92%","https://www.vec.vic.gov.au/-/media/8cf897b20b624d0faf1acc7ae470df89.pdf"],". At the ",["2022 election","https://www.vec.vic.gov.au/results/state-election-results/2022-state-election-results"],", that had fallen to just over 71%."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the current polling is accurate, then the 2026 election may well see the fragmented electorate consolidating around four main party groups: the Coalition, Labor, the Greens and One Nation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This has major implications for Victoria as the most progressive state in the country will have a centre-right government with a significant parliamentary presence for a party on the populist right. This will likely flow through to policy. For example, ",["the Coalition","https://theconversation.com/victorian-state-election-whats-at-stake-for-treaty-and-indigenous-self-determination-294873"]," and One Nation have pledged to abolish the Treaty with First Nations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lastly, the strong level of support for One Nation and the backlash against a Labor government that has been politically and electorally dominant points to more deep-seated issues of political dissatisfaction in Victoria that need to be addressed. For the most part, the campaign so far has not properly addressed these underlying issues."]}],"chars":5985},"https://theconversation.com/why-mark-carney-is-still-betting-big-on-europe-295647":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"dfa11ff94ef0da0e0850c92ce37ac2b3259ddb101eb8aefd1221f82b4b74c3ab","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-mark-carney-is-still-betting-big-on-europe-295647","bytes":182839,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why Mark Carney is still betting big on Europe","by":[{"n":"Katerina Sviderska","r":"PhD Candidate in Politics, University of Cambridge"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T14:25:55Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When European Union officials Ursula von der Leyen and Antonio Costa recently joined Mark Carney on the docks of Montréal’s Old Port for the Canada-EU Summit, Canada’s prime minister presented closer ties with the EU as a good deal for Canadian households."]},{"k":"p","s":["He argued a closer relationship promised ",["more choices and lower costs","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/10/30/canada-and-european-union-announce-new-alliance-future-create-greater"]," for families at a time when American tariffs ",["are causing pain","https://www.bankofcanada.ca/publications/mpr/mpr-2026-01-28/canadian-outlook/"]," on both sides of the Atlantic."]},{"k":"p","s":["In April 2025, my colleague, Léandre Benoit, and I ",["argued that the newly elected Carney would pursue a pragmatic and globally engaged liberalism","https://theconversation.com/what-liberal-mark-carneys-election-win-in-canada-means-for-europe-254775"],", definitively aligned with Europe. The Montréal summit confirms that alignment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The meeting’s firmest commitments concern democracy, while much of its economic measures are still to be carried out. With autocracies gaining ground around the world, and with Trump’s United States no longer a reliable ally — ",["although that may shift with the Democratic rout in the U.S. midterm elections","https://theconversation.com/blue-wave-the-democrats-historic-midterm-election-rout-could-also-offer-canada-a-path-to-peace-295834"]," — Canada and the EU have found in each other stable liberal partners who take democracy seriously."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What Liberal Mark Carney’s election win in Canada means for Europe","https://theconversation.com/what-liberal-mark-carneys-election-win-in-canada-means-for-europe-254775"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What Montréal delivered"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the economic side, the results of the summit are quite modest. Of the ",["20 measures","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2026/10/30/joint-statement-canada-and-european-union-building-together-alliance"]," announced, two are concluded agreements: one is a ",["digital trade agreement","https://www.canada.ca/en/global-affairs/news/2026/10/minister-sidhu-and-eu-commissioner-for-trade-and-economic-security-welcome-conclusion-of-canada-eu-digital-trade-agreement-negotiations.html"]," and the second is ",["a treaty","https://www.eib.org/en/press/all/2026-398-eib-and-canada-open-new-chapter-for-investment-at-eu-canada-summit"]," that lets the European Investment Bank finance Canadian critical minerals projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["The remaining measures are promises to be negotiated, for example on ",["the Erasmus+ education program","https://www.thestar.com/news/canada/canadian-students-would-get-access-to-eu-schools-under-new-deal-here-s-what-we-know/article_96e0827a-39c6-4a90-af46-b2e6af609cfe.html"]," and on ",["LNG exports","https://www.politico.eu/article/eu-and-canada-reach-agreement-on-critical-minerals-and-lng/"],". For a summit sold as offering relief for household budgets, few of these announcements will have an impact on Canadian kitchen tables any time soon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Left out of the final statement was the most ambitious and symbolic proposal: Carney ",["set June 2027","https://www.politico.eu/article/mark-carney-puts-deadline-on-eu-associate-membership-push/"]," as the deadline for Canada to become the European Union’s first “associate member,” a category that exists nowhere in EU law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["What Canada could gain from joining the EU’s Erasmus+ program, and what’s unresolved","https://theconversation.com/what-canada-could-gain-from-joining-the-eus-erasmus-program-and-whats-unresolved-292559"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Allies in defending democracy"]},{"k":"p","s":["The associate membership process is ",["driven by shared values","https://www.policymagazine.ca/what-canadas-associate-membership-in-the-eu-is-and-is-not/"],". Canada, one of the few established democracies to have avoided democratic backsliding, has strong institutions where no reforms are needed before it qualifies to be a partner of the EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even though the details of associate membership are still unclear, the partnership’s significance is in “ ",["elective affinity","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/speeches/2026/09/17/prime-minister-carney-delivers-address-european-parliament"],",” as Carney had set out in Strasbourg in September when addressing the European Parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["So far, ",["security and defence are where these shared values have produced concrete results","https://www.international.gc.ca/world-monde/international_relations-relations_internationales/eu-ue/security-defence-securite-defense.aspx?lang=eng"],". The joint statement warns that hybrid threats now target Canadian and European institutions, and it promises an early-warning system against foreign interference and disinformation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a clear acknowledgement that ",["Russian aggression goes beyond Ukraine","https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/where-and-how-putin-could-expand-his-war-in-europe-beyond-ukraine/"]," and that defending democracy has become a matter of national security. In the current global context where holding states accountable via international bodies is under threat — for example, the recent ",["American sanction of the International Criminal Court","https://www.icc-cpi.int/news/icc-strongly-rejects-us-sanctions-against-institution"]," — both the EU and Canada need each other more than ever in protecting their liberal values and their security."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["joint statement","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/statements/2026/10/30/joint-statement-canada-and-european-union-building-together-alliance"]," stretches Canada’s commitment along Europe’s whole eastern flank through the EU Common Security and Defence Policy, from the Arctic to the Black Sea, and frames it as a reinforcement of NATO."]},{"k":"h","s":["Beyond the balance sheet"]},{"k":"p","s":["While a Canada Pulse Insights poll found that ",["73 per cent of Canadians","https://nationalpost.com/news/canada/nearly-three-quarters-of-canadians-support-pm-in-seeking-closer-ties-with-europe/"]," support the idea of closer ties with the EU, the status of “associate member” is a problem in Europe."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Germany and several other member states oppose","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/european-union-canada"]," the label. At home, ",["Conservatives argue","https://www.conservative.ca/canada-eu-summit-did-nothing-for-canadians/"]," that the summit produced zero tariff removals or trade-barrier eliminations, and they’ve also raised concerns about what the agreement would mean for Canada’s independence and sovereignty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Judged on tariffs alone, the critics might have a point — after all, the EU cannot undo U.S.-imposed trade penalties. Diversifying away from Canada’s top trading partner demands both political will and time. In the meantime, the summit’s true value lies in the political message it sends."]},{"k":"p","s":["By offering a country outside Europe a place close to its family, the EU is saying that being European is as much a matter of values as of geography. If the process works, it could ",["become a model for other partners outside Europe","https://www.politico.eu/article/mark-carney-puts-deadline-on-eu-associate-membership-push/"],". For Canada, the membership would make clear to the U.S. and Canadian voters that the country has other partners and options beyond its southern neighbour."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Montréal summit gave Canada a safe harbour on the other side of the Atlantic. What holds the two partners together is a shared conviction that democracies must stand together as autocracies gain ground, beyond trade deals."]},{"k":"p","s":["By June 2027, we’ll know whether that conviction survives the doubts of some European capitals and whether Canada becomes the EU’s first associate member in name as well as in spirit."]}],"chars":4969},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"4232aafdb236277b439ad48f9079290c514acae6dd6c2184d8534fe13e06e402","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","bytes":58447,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Costa Rica travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-13T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and get ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Costa Rica’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Costa Rica set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Costa Rican Embassy in the UK","https://costaricanembassy.uk/embassy/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 1 day after the day you plan to leave Costa Rica."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Costa Rica without a visa for up to 180 days under a tourist visa waiver. The exact period is at the discretion of the immigration officer on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information on requirements or if you plan to work, or stay for a longer period, check with the ",["Costa Rican Embassy in the UK","https://costaricanembassy.uk/residence-categories/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay, the immigration authorities can fine you 100 US dollars for each month and refuse future applications to enter Costa Rica."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["When leaving the country by air, you may need to pay a departure tax of 29 US dollars. Most airlines include this in ticket prices. If you need to pay it, you can use cash or card."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Costa Rica, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Costa Rica guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/58/costa-rica#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Costa Rica","https://aduanafacil.hacienda.go.cr/AduanaFacil/Faq#viajando%20con%20equipaje"]," (in Spanish). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. If you try to remove wildlife from the country, including seashells, you could be fined."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Costa Rica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash, travellers cheques or goods if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money or goods could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Costa Rica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no history of terrorism in Costa Rica, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggings and theft are significant problems, particularly on the Atlantic coast. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of who is around you when using ATMs"]},{"k":"li","s":["be vigilant on buses and keep your luggage in view if possible – thieves are likely to try and distract you"]},{"k":"li","s":["watch wallets and valuables when on the beach"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid leaving luggage in a parked car, either in view or in the boot"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents where thieves slash a tyre and then offer to help change it, while an accomplice steals from the car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking alone in poorly lit or remote areas at night. Gangs occasionally carry out muggings and armed robberies. Gang-related violence, including shootings, has become more frequent in urban areas, including some locations popular with visitors. A number of foreign nationals including one British national have gone missing in recent years, with some incidents related to criminal activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re using a hire car, do not stop your car for strangers signalling for help – they could be carjackers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals sometimes cause deliberate collisions to stop vehicles and commit robberies or other crimes. If you think a collision was a deliberate act by another driver to make you stop, drive on until you reach a safe place like a police station or garage. You will need to be able to explain your actions to the traffic police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Spiked drinks and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rapes and sexual assaults have increased, some of which appear targeted toward tourists. Avoid leaving drinks unattended in bars as there have been reports of ‘spiked’ drinks resulting in assault and theft."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women travelling alone have reported having to pay extra attention to their personal safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Costa Rica."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs have apparently used methanol in the manufacture of cheap brands of local spirits, including vodka and ‘guaro’ (cane liquor). Take care when buying spirit-based drinks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a foreigner, you must carry ID such as a passport. The police will usually accept a printed copy. Make sure you have the original available somewhere safe in case they ask to see it."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not get involved with drugs of any kind. The Costa Rican authorities treat the possession of drugs and drug trafficking severely. The minimum sentence is 8 years imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Costa Rica is generally welcoming of LGBT+ travellers. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["While swimming on any beach in Costa Rica, bear in mind that rip currents are very common and there are often no lifeguards. Seek reliable local advice. Drownings are the second most common cause of accidental death and in recent years have averaged 50 to 60 per year, a third of whom were tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care if participating in tours involving snorkelling or similar activities. There have been recent fatalities."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular sightings of crocodiles along the Pacific coast near beaches popular with surfers, from Playa Azul down to Playa Esterillos, and there have been attacks in recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards for adventure activities and on small boats are variable. There have been several incidents involving small boats in the Tortuguero area, including a fatality due to a falling tree. If you plan to take part any of these activities, use an established company with experienced staff."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainforest tours and Adventure Tourism."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting jungle areas, go with an experienced local guide. There are fines for unauthorised entry into restricted conservation areas. Make sure you get appropriate insurance that covers you for all the activities you want to do. This includes activities such as quad biking, surfing, rock-climbing and zip-lining which can be hazardous but are frequently excluded from general travel insurance policies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Costa Rica, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private cars are only allowed to enter the capital of San José on certain weekdays, allocated using the last digit of the licence plate number. Your hire car company can give you more details."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Costa Rica for up to 180 days, depending on the length of stay you have been granted as a Tourist."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get an ",["international driving permit","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". Border authorities may refuse entry to right-hand drive vehicles as they’re illegal and do not qualify for local insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of driving is lower than in the UK. Drivers cause accidents by speeding, overtaking irresponsibly or ignoring traffic lights. Take care when approaching bridges over the road as these often narrow the road to a single lane."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are generally good on main routes. However, in the rainy season, heavy rains can cause potholes and landslides that block the roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident where somebody has been injured or where the other driver does not accept blame, you must not move your vehicle until the traffic police have arrived. Contact the traffic police (‘transito’ – telephone: 2222 9330 or 2222 9245) and the insurance investigator (INS – telephone: 800 800 8000) immediately."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using unofficial taxis (‘taxi piratas’). Official taxis are red (or orange at the airport) with a triangular sticker and plastic box on the roof with the name and number of the taxi company. It’s best to use radio-dispatched taxis. Make sure the driver’s ID is clearly visible on the dashboard and that the driver uses the meter."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Airport disruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Services at the Liberia Airport (LIR – Daniel Oduber International) in Guanacaste have been subject to interruptions. You should monitor carefully information from your travel provider when travelling to and from this airport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season usually runs from June to November – the same as the hurricane season in the Caribbean. Monitor the National Hurricane Center forecasts and the ",["World Meteorological Organization warnings","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/cgn/index.html"],". Follow the advice of local authorities, including any evacuation orders. Keep up to date with FCDO travel advice and social media. Plan any local travel carefully."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["The June-November period is also the peak rainy season. Flooding and landslides may occur, resulting in road closures and driving hazards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes: small tremors are frequent and movements greater than magnitude 6 occur periodically. Local infrastructure is well-prepared, and earthquakes seldom have widespread effects. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake or a tsunami."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Costa Rica has 16 volcanoes, several of which are considered active. The risk of eruptions is always present. There has recently been an increasing and significant series of eruptions at Poas Volcano."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check news reports and follow local advice before travelling to any areas around volcanoes. Avoid volcanic areas during and immediately after heavy rainfall when there’s increased risk of lava flows."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ash plumes can ",["affect air quality and have an impact on health","https://www.ivhhn.org/"],". If you have any pre-existing respiratory conditions, you might be at increased risk of triggering or worsening your symptoms. A properly fitted face mask may provide some protection."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Costa Rica, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Costa Rica guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/58/costa-rica#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See what health risks you’ll face in Costa Rica, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika Virus"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prescriptions from the UK cannot be used locally. To find a pharmacy (‘farmacia’) look for one of the big national chains such as Farmacia Fischel, Farmacia Sucre, FarmaValue, Farmacia Saba, or Farmacia Santa Lucia, among others; a quick search online should help you to identify the nearest one open."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Costa Rica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical care in Costa Rica is of a generally high standard. Ambulance services in remote areas may vary. Only initial emergency medical treatment is available without charge for visitors. Subsequent treatment will be charged. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Costa Rica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-costa-rica"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Costa Rica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Costa%20Rica"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Costa%20Rica"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Costa%20Rica"]," in Costa Rica"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Costa Rica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/costa-rica-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Costa Rica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/costa-rica-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/costa-rica/british-embassy-san-jose"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Costa Rica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-costa-rica"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15840,"change":"Updated information on customs rules; gang-related violence; fines for unauthorised entry into restricted conservation areas and earthquakes and recent volcanic activity ('Entry requirements' and 'Safety and security' pages)."},"https://theconversation.com/how-the-us-elections-and-iran-war-are-influencing-the-uns-cop31-climate-talks-and-discussions-around-fossil-fuels-296682":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"6dcd02b596cc09284ae0b7478293b862e9a09beb62e902411013408074fb2129","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-the-us-elections-and-iran-war-are-influencing-the-uns-cop31-climate-talks-and-discussions-around-fossil-fuels-296682","bytes":193576,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How the US elections and Iran war are influencing the UN’s COP31 climate talks – and discussions around fossil fuels","by":[{"n":"Jennifer Morgan","r":"Senior Fellow, Center for International Environment and Resource Policy and Climate Policy Lab, Tufts University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T20:31:35Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The 2026 United Nations climate talks are all about real-world impact. That’s evident as I listen to government officials and others from around the world at the ",["COP31 climate summit","https://cop31.tr/"]," in Antalya, Turkey."]},{"k":"p","s":["World leaders are seeing their countries suffer from ",["intensifying storms and heat fueled by climate change","https://wmo.int/resources/publication-series/state-of-climate-update-cop/state-of-climate-update-cop31"]," and from one of the ",["worst global energy crises","https://www.weforum.org/stories/energy-transition/world-facing-biggest-ever-energy-crisis-and-more-top-energy-stories"]," in history. A U.N. report found that global warming will ",["overshoot 1.5 degrees Celsius","https://www.unep.org/en/publications/report/limiting-overshoot-navigating-exceedance-15degc-and-pathways-towards-return"]," (2.7 degrees Fahrenheit), the level countries agreed a decade ago to try to avoid because of the growing risk of dangerous climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Middle East conflict has ",["intensified oil and gas price and supply volatility","https://www.iea.org/topics/the-middle-east-and-global-energy-markets"],", pushing economies to the brink as energy and food prices spike and energy security falters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Countries that rely on imported fossil fuels for their energy sources have borne the brunt of the energy crisis. Those doubling down on renewable energy are weathering the crisis better."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Pakistan, for example, the rapid expansion of solar power over the past six years helped the country avoid ",["more than US$12 billion","https://www.secureenergyproject.org/post/the-hedge-that-paid-off-how-pakistan-s-solar-boom-is-shielding-it-from-the-hormuz-crisis"]," in fossil fuel imports before the U.S. and Israel’s war with Iran began in February 2026. One forecast suggests solar could save the country ",["more than $6 billion more","https://www.secureenergyproject.org/post/the-hedge-that-paid-off-how-pakistan-s-solar-boom-is-shielding-it-from-the-hormuz-crisis"]," by the end of the year. Spain, which relies less on natural gas and ",["more on solar energy for electricity","https://www.iea.org/countries/spain/energy-mix"]," than most European countries, ",["kept electricity prices lower","https://ember-energy.org/latest-insights/latest-energy-shock-reminds-europe-of-its-risky-gas-reliance/"]," and avoided the worst of the gas-driven spikes seen in more exposed systems such as Italy’s."]},{"k":"p","s":["In formal negotiations and in meetings around the ",["U.N.’s broader Global Climate Action Agenda","https://www.climatechampions.net/our-work/action-agenda/"],", countries are working on ways to accelerate the use of clean energy and to provide poorer countries with the resources to adapt to climate change and expand clean energy."]},{"k":"p","s":["I have been following international climate negotiations for years as a former special climate envoy for Germany and ",["senior fellow","https://www.climatepolicylab.org/jennifer-morgan"]," at the Fletcher School at Tufts University. In 2026, after two years of the ",["Trump administration’s pressure","https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/27/climate/trump-international-pressure-climate-oil.html"]," to ",["get countries to abandon efforts to slow climate change","https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/06/climate/trump-climate-international-bullying.html"],", I’m seeing rising concern among leaders about the costs of fossil fuels on economies and people’s lives."]},{"k":"h","s":["The electrification solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["A step in transitioning away from fossil fuels is shifting to electrification powered by clean energy. The co-presidents of COP31, from Turkey and Australia, have proposed a global target of ",["35% of all energy use coming from electricity by 2035","https://cop31.tr/action-plan/clean-energy"]," – including for transportation and industry – and they are working to persuade other countries to sign on."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hitting that 35% mark could save fossil-fuel-importing countries ",["$400 billion a year","https://www.iea.org/files/435d1d9e-2814-44a2-b059-e080987e3c79/Electrification.pdf"],", according to the International Energy Agency. In consumer terms, $100 spent on electricity powers a car up to ",["three times farther","https://www.iea.org/reports/electrification"]," than $100 of gasoline, based on global averages. Reaching the goal could slash energy emissions across transportation, buildings and industry by ",["up to 55% by 2035","https://www.iea.org/reports/electrification"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the source of electrification matters. Forecasts from the International Renewable Energy Agency show that at least ",["78% of the electricity","https://www.irena.org/electrification"]," powering the world must come from renewable energy sources to keep global warming under the 1.5 C limit. Electrification delivers for both the climate and energy security if it runs on clean power instead of energy from oil, gas and coal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Getting the world to that point will require addressing some key barriers: the cost of infrastructure needed to deliver clean energy and the need for policies to encourage the changes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beyond the formal negotiations, countries are discussing multiple initiatives to provide ",["technical support to one another","https://greengridsinitiative.net/news/technical-assistance-hub-launched-at-cop31-to-accelerate-modernisation-of-electricity-grids"],", as countries develop power grids that can manage the variability of solar and wind power, and ",["financial help","https://www.electrifynow.world/news-and-resources/electrify-now-finance-coalition-launched-at-cop31"]," to countries that need it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Voters show their frustration with fossil fuels"]},{"k":"p","s":["The high financial and environmental costs of fossil fuels have been reshaping global politics. Voters came out in big numbers over the past few months to elect leaders who support clean, affordable energy solutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The world saw this notably with the ",["reelection of Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/11/brazil-election-cop-un-climate-lula-01161268"]," and the ",["biggest Democratic congressional victory","https://theconversation.com/epic-blue-wave-helps-democrats-take-congress-in-overwhelming-rebuke-to-president-trump-295830"]," in the United States in over three decades."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lula, in his first international trip after winning his fourth term, ",["called on the COP31 presidents","https://cop30.br/en/news-about-cop30/president-lula-brings-the-legacy-of-belem-to-cop31-urging-world-leaders-to-restore-climate-action-to-the-global-agenda"]," to carry forward Brazil’s work as host of COP30 on a ",["transition away from fossil fuels","https://theconversation.com/the-battle-over-a-global-energy-transition-is-on-between-petro-states-and-electro-states-heres-what-to-watch-for-in-2026-272205"],". He announced that Brazil will ",["host a future conference","https://theclimatewatch.com/lula-offers-to-host-future-fossil-fuel-transition-conference-in-brazil/"]," on the fossil fuel transition, following the first in Colombia in April 2026 and a second planned in 2027 in the island nation of Tuvalu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Brazil has clearly emerged as a climate superpower in Antalya. With its ",["greatest one-year reduction in deforestation","https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/deforestation-brazils-amazon-falls-lowest-record-202526-2026-10-16/"]," and its leadership in producing three plans, known as road maps, to help the world transition away from fossil fuels, end deforestation and ",["provide the $1.3 trillion","https://cop30.br/en"]," in financing needed for developing countries, Brazil has demonstrated it understands the urgency of the climate crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["We will see whether the co-presidents of COP31 will answer the calls from Lula and ",["U.N. Secretary-General António Guterres","https://webtv.un.org/en/asset/k13/k137pno7q4"]," to support these road maps becoming formal guidance for all countries."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Americans at COP31"]},{"k":"p","s":["California Gov. Gavin Newsom and a delegation of ",["18 members of the U.S. House of Representatives","https://www.seecinstitute.org/press/press-release-with-a-new-congress-on-the-horizon-18-us-lawmakers-arrive-at-cop31-to-signal-americas-return-to-sensible-climate-policynbsp"]," also came to COP31 to signal the presence of American leadership on future climate policy. President Donald Trump has ",["pulled the U.S. out","https://theconversation.com/damn-the-torpedoes-trump-ditches-a-crucial-climate-treaty-in-latest-move-to-dismantle-americas-climate-protections-273148"]," of the U.N. Framework Convention on Climate Change, the Paris Agreement and ",["dozens of other international organizations and treaties","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jan/12/trump-un-climate-treaty-unfccc"],". The U.S. did not send a formal delegation to the climate talks."]},{"k":"p","s":["As former U.S. climate envoy John Kerry ",["said in Antalya","https://transcripts.un.org/en/asset/k1b/k1brkp0hqo"],", “Americans did vote for clean, affordable energy, and they also voted for clean governance.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The international community will be watching to see whether the newly elected Democratic majority in Congress can help safeguard U.S. climate science after the ",["Trump administration’s extensive funding cuts","https://thebulletin.org/premium/2026-11/cuts-evictions-and-job-losses-a-view-from-the-trenches-of-climate-science-in-2026/"],", and whether it will restore critical ",["funding to international efforts","https://doi.org/10.1017/ajil.2025.10112"]," dealing with climate change."]},{"k":"h","s":["What success looks like"]},{"k":"p","s":["At COP31, the shift in the real-world politics of energy has dominated several events and the formal negotiations. But the countries ",["that are likely to lose","https://houseofsaud.com/saudi-cop31-fossil-fuel-roadmap-nov12/"]," from such a transition are also working diligently to ",["slow this transition","https://theconversation.com/5-ways-countries-stymie-climate-negotiations-without-actually-saying-no-295589"],". On the opening day, a coalition of oil-producing countries led by Saudi Arabia announced it ",["opposed any mention of Brazil’s road map","https://enb.iisd.org/antalya-un-climate-change-conference-cop31-daily-report-9nov2026"]," away from fossil fuels in the official COP31 agreement."]},{"k":"p","s":["For COP31 to be a success, the diplomatic process must demonstrate that it can catch up to the real economy and meet this moment of energy and climate crisis. I believe the summit’s final agreement should accelerate the electrification of infrastructure around the world and, at the same time, drive the transition away from fossil fuels in order to protect global security, economic stability and everyday citizens."]}],"chars":6945},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/dominica":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"bae8307b65db7228aeabb2b5cb25d8830dc06b4f63d3889b5e1da4c84b67dc6e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/dominica","bytes":45081,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Dominica travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-11T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:28:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/dominica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Dominica’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Dominica set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Dominica High Commission in the UK","https://www.dominicahighcommission.co.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Dominica, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa to visit Dominica. The border authorities will grant you a stay of 6 months on arrival. If you want to stay longer, you must arrange and pay for an extension with the ",["Dominica Immigration Division","https://nationalsecurity.gov.dm/divisions/immigration-division"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to overstay or work without a work permit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["At border control, you may also need to show a return or onward ticket."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a departure tax of 86 East Caribbean dollars or 33 US dollars. It is usually included in the cost of your plane ticket. You also need to pay departure tax if travelling by ferry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Dominica, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Dominica guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/66/dominica"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Dominica","https://customs.gov.dm/index.php/trade/prohibited-and-restricted-items"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Dominica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 East Caribbean dollars or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Dominica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Dominica, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations sometimes occur in Dominica. There have been instances of police using tear gas to disperse protesters. Should a demonstration occur, avoid the area concerned and exercise caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The crime rate in Dominica is low, but you could be at risk walking alone away from the main roads, particularly after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions to protect your personal safety:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure your accommodation is secure – this also applies if you’re staying on a yacht"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when walking alone off main roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["take particular care around large gatherings, including street and beach parties, especially after dark or during the festival season"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid isolated areas, including beaches, after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["only use licensed taxis"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not carry large amounts of cash or jewellery"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave valuables and travel documents in your hotel safe or a safety deposit box"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep car doors locked when driving and do not stop if pedestrians try to flag down your vehicle"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws on clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for anyone, including children, to dress in camouflage clothing."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug offences. Pack all your luggage yourself and do not carry anything through customs for anyone else."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes towards the LGBT+ community are mostly conservative throughout the Caribbean. Certain same-sex sexual acts are illegal. LGBT+ travellers should be mindful of local attitudes and be aware that they may receive unwanted and negative attention when showing affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming. Currents can be stronger than they look and not all beaches have lifeguards or warning flags."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before hiking to the Boiling Lake, check with guides that it is safe to do so. You can also contact the ",["Office of Disaster Management","https://odm.gov.dm/"]," or see their ",["Facebook updates","https://www.facebook.com/ODMDominica1"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You need to arrange car rental ahead of your arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must show your UK driving licence to get a temporary Dominican driving licence. Car hire companies will usually help with this."]},{"k":"p","s":["The roads on the island are sometimes narrow and in poor condition. Pedestrians often walk on the roads and drivers swerve to avoid potholes or fail to indicate before they pull out. There are few road signs and it’s easy to get lost. If you have an accident, call the police and do not move your vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["The main highway from Douglas Charles Airport is prone to landslides after bad weather and there are sheer drops where the road has fallen away. Avoid driving on this road at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis are not metered, but there are standard fares for most destinations. Registered taxis have a windscreen sticker that reads: ‘Nature Island’s Standard of Excellence’ followed by a number."]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid being overcharged, agree the fare before you set off. You can usually also pay in US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can tell your taxi driver if you want to be driven at slow speeds, but minibuses are likely to drive over the speed limit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season normally runs from June to November. Tropical storms and hurricanes can develop suddenly and unexpectedly. Monitor the US National Hurricane Center or the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/cgn/"]," for hurricane warnings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the ",["Government Information Service","https://news.gov.dm/"]," for local instructions, including any evacuation orders."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["During especially hot and dry periods a single spark or flame can start a wildfire. Report fires to the emergency services immediately."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Dominica and tremors are frequently felt. If there is an earthquake, local authorities should direct you. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Dominica","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/66/dominica#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Dominica","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/66/dominica"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Dominica"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Dominica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/dominica-list-of-medical-facilities-practitioners"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Dominica China Friendship Hospital, the government hospital in Roseau, can cope with many types of treatment, but serious cases may require emergency evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before choosing to be treated at a private facility, you should check the payment policy. Private clinics may ask for payment up front, so insurance documents may not be sufficient."]},{"k":"p","s":["Private medical treatment in Dominica can be expensive. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Dominica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Dominica"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Dominica"]," in Dominica"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Dominica","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-dominica"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Dominica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/dominica-prisoner-pack-2019/dominica-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/dominica/british-high-commission-bridgetown"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/dominica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":11104,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/21-years-after-disaster-helped-bring-peace-to-aceh-has-botched-indonesian-response-to-floods-reignited-calls-for-independence-290480":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"75d9a72f7437872ac71ab398080e0bd793fa4f49f7eb4f4346a81898ffc21b5a","read":"https://theconversation.com/21-years-after-disaster-helped-bring-peace-to-aceh-has-botched-indonesian-response-to-floods-reignited-calls-for-independence-290480","bytes":193434,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"21 years after disaster helped bring peace to Aceh – has botched Indonesian response to floods reignited calls for independence?","by":[{"n":"Azifah Astrina","r":"Ph.D. candidate in Political Science, University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign; Universitas Gadjah Mada"}],"pub":"2026-09-24T12:53:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Thousands gathered at Baiturrahman Grand Mosque in Banda Aceh on ",["Aug. 15, 2026","https://en.tempo.co/read/2117590/aceh-peace-day-tribute-turns-violent-as-crowd-clashes-with-police"],", to commemorate ",["21 years","https://theacehpost.com/news/bendera-merah-putih-di-pendopo-gubernur-aceh-diturunkan-massa-berkibar-bulan-bintang/index.html"]," of peace between Indonesia and the separatist Free Aceh Movement, or GAM."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some participants raised GAM’s red, black and white crescent-star flag and chanted “Free Aceh,” while others lowered Indonesia’s national flag and replaced it with the former separatist movement’s flag."]},{"k":"p","s":["These were politically significant acts in a province where GAM fought a nearly ",["three-decade","https://media.defense.gov/2025/Apr/07/2003683780/-1/-1/0/20250407_INDONESIA_ACEH_1976-2005%20_FINAL.PDF"]," armed struggle for independence before the 2005 Helsinki agreement ended the conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["And the Aug. 15 display was not an isolated incident. In ",["December 2024","https://www.thejakartapost.com/indonesia/2024/12/05/gams-crescent-and-star-flag-raised-in-lhoukseumawe"],", former GAM members raised the crescent-star flag during the movement’s anniversary, with one former combatant expressing hope that it would eventually fly across Aceh. The flag appeared publicly again in ",["December 2025","https://en.tempo.co/read/2076220/tni-disperses-crowds-flying-gam-flags-in-acehs-lhokseumawe"],", at which point Indonesian soldiers dispersed crowds displaying it."]},{"k":"p","s":["The return of these independence symbols and slogans comes as Aceh continues to recover from severe floods and landslides that struck the province in late ",["November 2025","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/death-toll-rises-to-164-after-floods-and-landslides-on-indonesias-sumatra-island"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["A different natural disaster, the 2004 tsunami, ",["helped create conditions","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geoforum.2007.10.010"]," that accelerated the peace process between Aceh and Jakarta. Yet two decades later, it is ",["criticism","https://news.mongabay.com/2026/06/survivors-sue-indonesian-government-over-response-to-catastrophic-sumatra-floods/"]," of the central government’s response to the latest emergency that has served to intensify expressions of independence."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["scholar of nationalism and political geography","https://pol.illinois.edu/directory/profile/astrina2"],", I see the resurgence of pro-independence sentiment in Aceh not simply as evidence that separatism is returning, but also as a reminder that national belonging is continually negotiated between states and citizens, and can be harmed by perceived neglect in times of need."]},{"k":"p","s":["That matters beyond Aceh. The peace agreement transformed a bloody separatist conflict into one of Southeast Asia’s best examples of ",["post-conflict reconciliation","https://globalsouthforum.org/article/aceh-at-the-crossroads-hope-for-peace-and-political-challenges-in-a-new-era"],". Renewed tensions would raise questions not only about Aceh’s relationship with Indonesia, but also the durability of a peace settlement that has held for more than two decades."]},{"k":"h","s":["Peace ended war, not nationalism"]},{"k":"p","s":["GAM’s struggle was about more than opposition to policies made in Jakarta. Founded in 1976, the movement presented Aceh — located on the island of Sumatra at the westernmost edge of Indonesia — as a distinct nation that should be independent from Indonesia. GAM drew on Acehnese history to portray independence ",["as the restoration","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," of a sovereignty that had existed when Aceh was an independent sultanate. The nearly three-decade conflict ",["killed thousands","https://reliefweb.int/report/indonesia/no-peace-without-justice-victims-indonesia%E2%80%99s-aceh-conflict-demand-truth-justice-and"],". Civilians bore much of the violence, with Indonesian security forces and GAM both ",["implicated in abuses","https://www.hrw.org/news/2005/05/27/acehs-forgotten-victims"],", including torture, arbitrary arrests, extortion and forced displacement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The devastating tsunami of 2004 ",["acted as a catalyst to peace","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.geoforum.2007.10.010"],", shining a light on the suffering of Aceh’s population while opening the doors to international aid and presence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The armed conflict officially ended with the signing of the ",["2005 Helsinki","https://peacemaker.un.org/sites/default/files/document/files/2024/05/id050815memorandum20of20understanding.pdf"]," agreement, but it did not make Acehnese nationalism disappear. Instead, it made room for Aceh’s political distinctiveness within Indonesia. The agreement gave Aceh extensive self-governing powers, allowing local political parties, expanding political representation and granting the region the authority to enact provincial laws. Substantial discretion over economic affairs and natural resources was handed to Aceh, although lingering grievances over ",["revenue-sharing provisions related to the province’s gas fields","https://www.jstor.org/stable/27638587"]," remain to this day."]},{"k":"p","s":["The political settlement largely succeeded in ending the organized armed campaign for independence."]},{"k":"p","s":["GAM disarmed, and many of its former leaders ",["moved into","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/186810341002900105"]," electoral politics, forming local parties and winning positions in Aceh’s government and legislature. But while the armed movement ended, pro-independence ideas and symbols did not disappear entirely."]},{"k":"p","s":["That distinction matters because peace did not depend on Acehnese abandoning their distinct political identity and simply becoming Indonesian; it depended on changing the terms of their relationship with Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Aceh could remain part of the country while retaining considerable control over its own political affairs. In that sense, Helsinki did more than end a war. It created political conditions that made remaining within Indonesia acceptable."]},{"k":"h","s":["From disaster to independence talk"]},{"k":"p","s":["The November 2025 floods and landslides killed ",["more than 1,000 people","https://thediplomat.com/2025/12/acehs-bitter-lesson-relearned/"]," and forced more than 1 million to relocate. Aceh was among the hardest-hit provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["It brought citizens into much more direct contact with the Indonesian government and made people dependent on public authorities for assistance and recovery."]},{"k":"p","s":["Calls for Jakarta to designate the floods and landslides a ",["national disaster","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-desakan-penetapan-bencana-nasional-di-sumatera-terus-mengalir-dari-aceh"]," began soon after they struck, but President Prabowo Subianto rejected them, arguing that Indonesia had sufficient capacity to manage the crisis. Prabowo’s rejection of foreign aid, in particular, led to ",["widespread anger in Aceh","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgzwqjpzp4o"]," and provided a strong contrast to the response in 2004, when international assistance was crucial to the post-tsunami effort."]},{"k":"p","s":["Almost a year later, significant challenges persist in Aceh. As of Sept. 7, 2026, only ",["649 of the 34,777 permanent homes","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5730356/satgas-prr-catat-649-unit-hunian-tetap-di-aceh-telah-rampung"]," needed for those displaced had been completed. The latest available data also showed that 93 regional road segments remained nonfunctional, while only 188 of 676 bridges had been restored as of ",["Aug. 8","https://dialeksis.com/aceh/sembilan-bulan-pascabencana-warga-aceh-masih-menunggu-rumah-dan-akses-permanen/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On ",["Aug. 14","https://en.tempo.co/read/2117590/aceh-peace-day-tribute-turns-violent-as-crowd-clashes-with-police"]," – one day before the GAM flag event – a civil-society coalition again raised white flags and called on Jakarta to declare the disaster a national disaster."]},{"k":"p","s":["But why do grievances over the government’s response turn into pro-independence talk in Aceh?"]},{"k":"p","s":["History offers part of the answer. A strong Acehnese identity has not always meant wanting to leave Indonesia. ",["Acehnese leaders","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," supported Indonesian independence from the Dutch colonial empire in 1945, and even the ",["Darul Islam rebellion","https://media.defense.gov/2024/Mar/20/2003416575/-1/-1/0/20240306_DARULISLAM_1949-62.PDF"]," of the 1950s – which sought to transform Indonesia into an Islamic state – did not seek an independent Acehnese country. Opposition to Dutch colonial rule, followed by Islamic networks and solidarity, ",["helped connect","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," Acehnese elites to the wider Indonesian political community."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was only later, as relations with the central government deteriorated, that independence became the goal."]},{"k":"p","s":["This history suggests that Acehnese nationalism is not a fixed political force that periodically resurfaces unchanged. Different understandings of the nation can ",["compete and be renegotiated","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8129.2007.00277.x"]," as political conditions change. Acehnese and Indonesian national identities are therefore not necessarily mutually exclusive; their relationship has changed as the political relationship between Aceh and Jakarta has changed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The return of “Free Aceh” chants and GAM-associated symbols shows that, more than two decades after the peace agreement, independence remains available as a political language for expressing dissatisfaction with Indonesia — especially in moments like natural disasters that have hurt ",["government legitimacy","https://doi.org/10.1111%2Fgove.12440"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nationalism as a two-way process"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more than two decades, Aceh has remained peaceful and within Indonesia, while retaining extensive autonomy and a distinct political identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the continued use of “Free Aceh” slogans and separatist symbols shows that belonging to Indonesia is not simply settled by peace, autonomy or the passage of time. Nor can nationalism be understood simply by looking at how countries build identity through ",["schools, maps, flags and ceremonies","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1111/nana.70002"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rather, nationalism works both ways: Indonesia promotes a shared identity, but Acehnese also negotiate what belonging to Indonesia means through their interaction with the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps the more important question, then, is not why independence talk has returned, but what has kept Aceh within Indonesia for the past 21 years."]}],"chars":7784},"https://theconversation.com/novaya-gazeta-lived-here-russias-media-ecosystem-has-been-slowly-dismantled-over-the-past-decade-296742":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"98420f752357e86bb4078a4ecec5c2b48c2c2ffad776c4d317ae76e9549d7a51","read":"https://theconversation.com/novaya-gazeta-lived-here-russias-media-ecosystem-has-been-slowly-dismantled-over-the-past-decade-296742","bytes":181949,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Novaya Gazeta lived here’: Russia’s media ecosystem has been slowly dismantled over the past decade","by":[{"n":"Chloe Arnold Lowe","r":"PhD Candidate in International Politics, Aberystwyth University"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:42:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["There was no dramatic raid and no armed police storming the building to make multiple arrests. The end of Novaya Gazeta, one of Russia’s last remaining independent newspapers, was more humdrum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drawers were emptied, files packed away and a sign was hastily nailed above the entrance to the paper’s central ",["Moscow","https://theconversation.com/topics/russia-1376"]," office on November 9. It read simply: “Novaya Gazeta lived here.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more than three decades, ",["Novaya Gazeta","https://theconversation.com/nobel-peace-prize-how-dmitry-muratov-built-russias-bravest-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-169560"]," had exposed corruption, investigated abuses of power and provided a home for some of Russia’s bravest reporters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Six journalists associated with the paper were ",["murdered","https://theconversation.com/ukraine-war-reports-suggest-that-russia-has-been-deliberately-targeting-journalists-which-is-a-war-crime-213663"]," for their work, among them ",["Anna Politkovskaya","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/oct/05/ten-years-putin-press-kremlin-grip-russia-media-tightens"],", whose reporting on the war in Chechnya reached far beyond Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Announcing the closure, the paper’s co-founder and recipient of the 2021 Nobel peace prize, Dmitry Muratov, did not mince his words."]},{"k":"p","s":[["He told reporters","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/9/russian-investigative-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-closes-citing-govt-clampdown"]," gathered to witness the closure of the Moscow newsroom: “Those in our country who advocate for peace have been denied the right to read what they choose.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many commentators have treated the closure as the death of independent media in Russia. But that interpretation misses a bigger story."]},{"k":"p","s":["The end of Novaya Gazeta is significant not just because one newspaper has closed, but because it was one of the last survivors of a much broader independent media ecosystem that has been slowly dismantled over the past decade."]},{"k":"h","s":["A steady erosion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia did not lose its independent media in a single act of repression. Long before the closure of Novaya Gazeta, the authorities had already weakened or sidelined many of the organisations that once dominated independent reporting."]},{"k":"p","s":["TV Rain, RBK, Vedomosti, Lenta.ru and Meduza, to name just a few, all faced different forms of pressure. Some experienced ownership changes. Others lost access to audiences, investors or advertisers. Many were forced into exile."]},{"k":"p","s":["The methods varied, but the result was the same: the steady erosion of editorial independence."]},{"k":"p","s":["That process emerges clearly from interviews I conducted with leading Russian journalists for my doctoral research earlier in 2026. One of them, Svetlana Reiter, rejected the idea that independent media disappeared overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["Looking back, she reflected that “everything happened in steps”. Small changes accumulated over time, often appearing manageable in isolation but gradually transforming the environment in which journalists worked."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another journalist, Ilya Barabanov, traced the beginning of the shift to 2012, when protests erupted ",["following alleged fraud","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-europe-58614227"]," in parliamentary elections. These elections saw Vladimir Putin return to the presidency having previously stepped aside to serve as prime minister since 2008."]},{"k":"p","s":["Barabanov recalled that, during the presidency of Dmitry Medvedev, “there had been a feeling that perhaps the country would follow some sort of civilised path of development”. Those hopes vanished after Putin’s return."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Everything went wrong in 2012,” Barabanov told me. “That’s when it became clear that everything was going to go in a completely different direction.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The turning point came in 2014. Internationally, the year is remembered for Russia’s annexation of Crimea. Inside Russia’s independent media, many reporters remember something else: the removal of ",["Galina Timchenko","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-europe-26543464"]," as editor of Lenta.ru, then one of the country’s most influential news websites."]},{"k":"p","s":["The publication itself survived, but dozens of journalists resigned in protest. One of them, Ilya Azar, later described the decision bluntly to me in an interview: “That was direct censorship.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The significance of the affair lay in what it revealed. The state did not need to close media organisations outright. Pressure could be applied through owners, regulators and business interests. Editorial independence could be weakened without banning publications or imprisoning journalists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the following years, the same pattern would appear repeatedly across the Russian media landscape. Journalists increasingly found themselves fighting not only for the right to publish stories, but for the survival of the institutions that allowed those stories to be reported in the first place."]},{"k":"p","s":["From that perspective, the closure of Novaya Gazeta looks less like a sudden death and more like the final chapter in a much longer story."]},{"k":"p","s":["Together with other tenacious, independent news organisations, the paper formed an ecosystem that once reached millions of Russians and offered an alternative to state-controlled narratives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022, and the introduction of laws that label journalists as ",["foreign agents","https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/12/01/russia-new-restrictions-foreign-agents"]," who face up to 15 years in prison for reporting on the war, that ecosystem has largely disappeared from Russia itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["But it has not vanished entirely. Many of the journalists who built it continue to report from abroad through media organisations in exile. In that sense, the story of Russian independent journalism is not simply one of suppression. It is also a story of adaptation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The lights may have gone out in the Moscow newsroom of Novaya Gazeta, but the traditions the newspaper represented endure."]}],"chars":5057}};
